class:: PitchDeviation
summary:: Signed cents deviation from a reference or tuning grid
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Pitch
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Pitch2, Classes/FundamentalCandidates

description::
Uses the logarithmic frequency-ratio definition of musical cents. The previous mode compares consecutive control blocks and resets its reference on an unvoiced block. Reference mode accepts a changing frequency, so a custom tuning system can supply its selected reference externally. There is no internal pitch estimation or smoothing.

Vanilla link::Classes/UnaryOpUGen:: frequency-to-MIDI arithmetic can express the same cents conversion. This class also supplies reference/grid/previous policies and explicit undefined-input behavior.

classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: freq
Control-rate frequency in Hz; invalid or nonpositive values return zero.

argument:: reference
Positive reference in Hz. In nearest12TET mode it anchors the equal-tempered grid; another reference can establish a custom anchor.

argument:: mode
One of \reference (1200 * log2(freq/reference)), \nearest12TET (nearest 100-cent grid point), or \previous (previous control-block frequency).

returns::
Signed deviation in cents. Positive is sharp; negative is flat. Exact half-semitone ties use round-away-from-zero in the grid index.

examples::
Compare the detected intonation at left with its nearest equal-tempered pitch at right. Boot the server before evaluation. The short fade masks analysis warmup.
code::
(
Routine({
    var buffer = Buffer.read(s, ExampleFiles.child);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2PitchExample = {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, buffer, BufRateScale.kr(buffer), loop: 1);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);
        var pitch = PitchMPM.kr(source, 80, 1200, 4096);
        var cents = PitchDeviation.kr(pitch[0]);
        var snapped = pitch[0] * (cents.neg / 100).midiratio;
        var original = SinOsc.ar(pitch[0].max(20), 0, pitch[1] * pitch[2] * 0.07);
        var quantized = SinOsc.ar(snapped.max(20), 0, pitch[1] * pitch[2] * 0.07);
        var sound = [original + source * 0.08, quantized + source * 0.08];
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.25)
    }.play;
    ~mir2PitchBuffer = buffer;
}).play(AppClock);
)
::

Stop and release the example:
code::
(
~mir2PitchExample.free;
~mir2PitchBuffer.free;
 )
::

